  "query_preview": "..\n(Tomorrow through Monday)\nIssued at 1151 AM CDT Mon Aug 10 2026\n\nThe upper level ridging pattern will fluctuate in the coming days\nbut the end result for our area is more or less the same: hot and\ndry. Ridging thus far has been centered over the four corners \nregion and across the SE U.S. with positive height anomalies \nremaining in place between the two. As we move into mid-late week,\nwestern ridging will tend to shift east and merge with the SE \nridge. This opens the door for a weak cold front to move into the \ncentral Plains towards our CWA. However, latest guidance has \ncontinued to suggest the front will remain north of us with fewer \nsensible impacts for E OK and NW AR. Model output does indicate at\nleast a slight chance of rain near the KS and MO borders late \nthis weekend, but overall dry conditions are forecast to continue.\n\nIn the lower levels, lee troughing will provide persistent south-\nsouthwest winds over the coming days. These winds will become \nbreezy during the afternoon hours and do not fully dissipate \novernight. With this orientation, we should see dewpoints mix out \nmore than previous days, especially mid to late week. However, \ntemperatures will also increase slightly during this time. \nOverall, afternoon temperatures near/above 100 and maximum heat \nindex values greater than 105 will remain likely for much of the \narea. Based on trends so far this morning and Sunday afternoon, \nhave issued a Heat Advisory for the same areas on Tuesday. \nAdditional heat headlines are likely over the coming days. Please \ncontinue to take precautions to stay safe when outdoors this week.",
